## One-Time Setup (5 minutes)

You only need to do this once. After setup, the tool is ready every time you open the project.

**Step 1 — Open Claude.ai and go to your Projects**

Log into claude.ai. In the left sidebar, look for a **Projects** section. Click **New Project**.

**Step 2 — Name your project**

Give it a clear name — "AWSM Strategy Tool" or "Draper" works well. Add a short description if you like.

**Step 3 — Open the system prompt file**

Open `draper-system-prompt.md` on your computer. Select all the text (Ctrl+A on Windows, Cmd+A on Mac) and copy it.

**Step 4 — Paste into Project Instructions**

Inside your new project, look for the **Instructions** section on the right side of the screen. Click the **+** button next to it. A text area will open. Paste everything you copied into that text area.

**Step 5 — Save**

Save the instructions. Your project is now configured. You won't need to do this again.

